                "content": "Based on your project structure, I can see you're learning Terraform and have various components. Let me guide you toward building something practical and valuable that you'll use daily.\n\n## Here's my recommendation for a real-world project:\n\n**Build a Personal Development Infrastructure** - A complete, production-ready environment that includes:\n\n1. **Multi-tier Web Application Stack**\n   - VPC with public/private subnets across multiple AZs\n   - Application Load Balancer\n   - Auto Scaling Group for EC2 instances\n   - RDS database (PostgreSQL/MySQL)\n   - ElastiCache for caching\n   - S3 for static assets\n   - CloudFront CDN\n\n2. **CI/CD Pipeline Infrastructure**\n   - CodePipeline + CodeBuild\n   - ECR for Docker images\n   - ECS/EKS for container orchestration\n\n3. **Monitoring & Logging**\n   - CloudWatch dashboards\n   - SNS for alerts\n   - Lambda for automated responses\n\n4. **Security & Compliance**\n   - WAF rules\n   - Security groups with proper segmentation\n   - IAM roles following least privilege\n   - Secrets Manager for credentials\n\n## Why this approach?\n\n- **Daily use**: You can deploy your own projects/apps\n- **Learning depth**: Covers networking, compute, storage, security\n- **Modular**: Reusable modules you can mix and match\n- **Cost-aware**: Can be scaled down for learning, up for production\n- **Portfolio-worthy**: Shows real-world skills\n\n## Let's start step by step:\n\n**Phase 1**: Should we start with the networking foundation (VPC, subnets, routing)?\n\n**Phase 2**: Add compute layer (EC2, ASG, ALB)\n\n**Phase 3**: Add data layer (RDS, ElastiCache, S3)\n\n**Phase 4**: Add observability (CloudWatch, SNS)\n\n**Phase 5**: Add CI/CD automation\n\nWould you like to start with Phase 1 - building a robust, reusable VPC module? I'll guide you through creating something production-grade but understandable."
